    "problem": "This paper addresses the challenge of attributing ocean temperature change by attempting the first three-signal separation of influences from greenhouse gases, anthropogenic aerosols, and natural forcings, which is improved by analyzing the combined temporal, vertical, and geographical structure of the warming signal.",
    "method": "This study applies an optimal fingerprinting method using fingerprints of ocean temperature change that incorporate temporal, vertical, and geographical structure to simultaneously attribute observed warming to greenhouse gas, anthropogenic aerosol, and natural forcings.",
    "task": "The task is to determine whether observed ocean temperature changes from 1960\u20132005 can be attributed to anthropogenic (greenhouse gas, aerosols) and natural forcings by comparing observational datasets with CMIP5 climate model simulations.",
